{"name":"Sensual Climax","hex":"#da3287","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sensual","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Inducing pleasurable or erotic sensations.","Of or pertaining to the physical senses; sensory."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensual"},{"term":"climax","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rhetorical device in which a series is arranged in ascending order.","An instance of such an ascending series."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reach or bring to a climax (in any sense).","To form the climax to; to be the climax of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climax"}],"entries":[{"title":"Climax (2018 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Climax is a 2018 experimental psychological horror film directed, written and co-edited by Gaspar Noé. Featuring an ensemble cast of 24 actors, led by Sofia Boutella, the plot is set in 1996 and follows a French dance troupe holding a days-long rehearsal in an abandoned school; the final night of rehearsing is a success, but the group's celebratory after-party takes a dark turn when the communal bowl of sangria is spiked with LSD, sending each of the dancers into agitated, confused and psychotic states."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Climax_%282018_film_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climax_(2018_film)","wikidata":"Q52000412"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Climax_%282018_film_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Climax_%282018_film_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClimax_(2018_film_poster).jpg"}],"sounds":{"sensual":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://uploa